course: dictionary
lesson: 2819
title: A disturbance breaks the calm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A «disturbance» is something that breaks into a calm time or place. It stops you resting, working or thinking. «The loud drilling was a disturbance all morning, so I could not rest.» The drilling broke the quiet, so it was a disturbance.
explain: The word can also mean trouble. «The police were called to a disturbance outside the club.» Here people were fighting or causing trouble in a public place. Ask yourself: was something calm or normal changed or interrupted? If yes, disturbance probably fits.
explain: Look for useful phrases. You can «cause a disturbance», or say «sorry for the disturbance» when you interrupt someone. In UK news, «disturbances» can mean riots, which are large groups of people causing trouble together.
fact: A disturbance is something that interrupts, upsets or breaks a calm time.
fact: «Disturbance» can mean a noise that stops you resting or working.
fact: «Disturbance» can mean trouble or fighting in a public place.
fact: «Disturbance» can also mean a change or upset in something normal, such as a disturbance in the weather.
fact: In UK news, «disturbances» can mean riots.
exercise: «The loud drilling was a disturbance all morning.» What was the disturbance? | *A noise that stopped people resting | A happy party with music | A cool breeze through the window | A kind of drill used for holes
exercise: «The police were called to a disturbance outside the club.» What kind of disturbance was this? | A sleepy afternoon | A change in the weather | A quiet walk in the park | *Trouble or fighting in a public place
exercise: Which phrase means you are sorry for interrupting someone? | happy for the noise | sorry for the calm | *sorry for the disturbance
test: «There was a sleep disturbance because the dog barked all night.» What does sleep disturbance mean? | A dream about dogs | A bed made of wood | A very deep and long sleep | *Something that stopped sleep from being calm
test: Mia says disturbance is just another word for storm. Why is she wrong? | Disturbance means exactly storm and nothing else | Disturbance means a sunny day | *A storm can be one kind of disturbance, but the word can also mean noise or trouble
exam: Which sentence uses disturbance correctly? | Disturbance the sun shone brightly | *The alarm was a disturbance that woke the whole street | I disturbance my cat every morning with a sandwich | The disturbance was a red apple on the table
